  designNotes: 'Beat 10: a clock, and the beat chart names its length - "armor in
    2 turns". The lead is 2 rather than 1 for that reason: one turn is a heads-up
    you can only brace for, two is long enough to change what you are shooting at
    and still have a volley left to do it with, which is the whole "kill priority
    vs clock" beat. The strip counts down live (2 turns, then 1 turn) because a warning
    holding the same number for two turns says the clock has stopped. This is the
    first level in the project to fire a ReinforcementWave; its telegraph and announcement
    were imported and displayed nowhere from the port until Phase F.'
